WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Drop a steel bolt into the sea.

2
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.780
It sinks straight to the bottom.

3
00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.740
Yet a ship with a steel hull,
far heavier than any bolt,

4
00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.470
rides on the surface.

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.430
Water pushes up on anything placed in it.

6
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.780
So why does that push win for
the ship, but lose for the bolt?

7
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.290
What decides which one floats?

8
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.410
In this mission, you'll lower a
stone on a spring balance into water,

9
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.330
and watch the reading fall.

10
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.250
Then you'll hold a foam ball
under water on a string,

11
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.050
and work out the pull on that string.

12
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:37.250
Your mission: explain what decides
whether a steel object floats or sinks.
